* L7812 positive 12V linear regulator -- behavioral fallback model.
*
* ST's encrypted/vendor L78xx SPICE subckt was not available on this machine, so
* per the Tier 1 plan this is a behavioral stand-in: a 12V regulated output that
* collapses into dropout when the input rail sags. It models the two things the
* Tier 1 DC checks care about -- regulation setpoint and dropout -- but does NOT
* model current limit, thermal foldback, quiescent current, or line/load
* transient response. Keep that in mind when reading ldo_reg.cir results.
*
* Dropout: ~2V is the L7812 datasheet worst case (Vin-Vout at 1A). Modeled here as
* a fixed 2V term, so Vout = min(12, Vin - 2). Below Vin=14V the part is in dropout
* and the output simply follows the input minus 2V.
*
* Pins:  IN  OUT  GND
.subckt L7812 IN OUT GND
BREG OUT GND V = min(12, V(IN,GND) - 2)
.ends L7812
